  "conclusion": "The pose-free photometric check is bounded and discriminates wide-baseline candidates much more strongly than adjacent candidates. The first adjacent mapping experiment also filtered registration support and is therefore retained only as a superseded methodological negative. A corrected 32-128-frame experiment keeps registration support intact and preserves 9,998 images, but explicit wide metric tracks score 0.39004/0.77557 m RMSE/p95 versus the 0.38754/0.76836 m visloc control. Independent support exists, but adding it as ordinary reprojection tracks does not repair the remaining gauge drift. Direct metric factors are also rejected: a 2-degree stereo 3-D-to-3-D gate yields 200 clean fits only at the start, while a one-sided stereo-PnP formulation yields 398 sensor- and bidirectionally-consistent pairs but none in frames 2,500-3,499. Lowering observability gates reaches later frames only by admitting mutually inconsistent direction and scale."
